From: LeonMobile developers <developers@leonmobile.local>
Subject: [PATCH] ArmVirt: avoid firmware TRNG calls on the QEMU reference board

The reference target runs QEMU 6.2 and a Cortex-A72 without an SMCCC TRNG
backend. Probing SMCCC_VERSION via HVC raises an undefined-instruction
exception before the boot manager can run on that emulator. Use the null
ArmTrngLib (which returns unsupported) and provide actual entropy through
VirtioRngDxe and the mandatory virtio-rng-pci device instead. This does not
replace entropy with timer or software pseudo-random output.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LeonMobile QEMU reference board policy]
Signed-off-by: LeonMobile developers <developers@leonmobile.local>
---
--- a/ArmVirtPkg/ArmVirt.dsc.inc
+++ b/ArmVirtPkg/ArmVirt.dsc.inc
@@ -147,7 +147,7 @@
   OpensslLib|CryptoPkg/Library/OpensslLib/OpensslLibCrypto.inf
 !endif
   RngLib|MdePkg/Library/BaseRngLib/BaseRngLib.inf
-  ArmTrngLib|ArmPkg/Library/ArmTrngLib/ArmTrngLib.inf
+  ArmTrngLib|MdePkg/Library/BaseArmTrngLibNull/BaseArmTrngLibNull.inf
   ArmMonitorLib|ArmPkg/Library/ArmMonitorLib/ArmMonitorLib.inf
 
   #
